WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.409 --> 00:00:04.450
Jordan Peele's record-breaking horror hit
Get Out is a socially conscious thriller that

00:00:04.450 --> 00:00:08.189
deals with the worst modern boogeyman of them
all: racism.

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:11.929
With a number one debut at the box office
and a record-breaking performance on multiple

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:16.040
fronts, Get Out is a film to be remembered
— and we're here to tell you its untold

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.040
truth.

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:20.380
Fair warning: now's your chance to look away
if you don't want spoilers.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.140
It's not about the president

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:26.210
Get Out might seem like a response to our
current, super-charged political climate,

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:31.310
but Jordan Peele was working on the idea even
before Barack Obama was elected — and afterward,

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:36.440
he was intrigued by the country's so-called
"post-racial ideal", in which people seemed

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:41.120
to believe that a black President represented
the total defeat of racism in the United States.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.780
Peele wrote Get Out as a response — to show
that not all racists look like cross-burning

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:46.780
Klan members.

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:54.020
"The original idea with the movie was to point
out this very real horror we haven't gotten

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:55.020
over."

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:56.840
It's a tribute to classic horror

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:01.440
Peele took inspiration for Get Out from other
scary movies about seemingly well-meaning

00:01:01.449 --> 00:01:06.280
people doing horrible things — like Rosemary's
Baby and The Stepford Wives.

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:10.560
But the classic slasher franchise Halloween
also worked its way in — not that there's

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:15.290
a masked killer in Peele's film, but both
movies make the white picket fences of suburbia

00:01:15.290 --> 00:01:17.270
look awfully sinister.

00:01:17.270 --> 00:01:20.510
Jordan Peele dreamed up the film's scariest
scene

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:25.510
Grab a fresh pair of underpants, because we're
about to relive one of this movie's freakiest

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:26.440
interludes.

00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:35.320
This secret behind this creepy moment?

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:39.900
It's straight out of Jordan Peele's subconscious,
based on a dream he had about walking through

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.280
a room of people who all fell silent as soon
as he turned the corner — which makes this

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:47.050
scene literal nightmare material.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.360
The original ending was much darker

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:52.930
If you thought that the siren and strobe light
in this scene meant the cops were coming to

00:01:52.930 --> 00:01:56.190
take Chris away, you're in good company — with
the film's director.

00:01:56.190 --> 00:02:00.630
"The first ending that I scripted was not
as happy."

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:05.410
Originally, Peele ended Get Out with Chris
taking the fall for murdering Rose's family

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:09.690
— but fortunately, he changed his mind,
deciding that it made more sense for Chris

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:10.690
to come out on top.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:16.440
"I was so excited when I was able to go get
the money to go reshoot the ending that I

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.510
knew would really work.”

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.200
It's a record breaker

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.440
Get Out was an instant success at the box
office, taking first place in its opening

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:29.350
weekend despite strong competition from both
a beloved superhero and a film where Samuel

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.070
L. Jackson battles a giant gorilla.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.940
But more importantly, Jordan Peele is the
first African-American writer and director

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:41.490
to helm a debut film that made over $100 million
— and Get Out hit that benchmark faster

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.030
than any Blumhouse picture in history.

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.990
It's in the zeitgeist

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:50.411
Rave reviews and box office records are all
well and good, but the true measure of a movie's

00:02:50.411 --> 00:02:54.290
importance is whether it spawns a meme — like
the Get Out challenge.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:58.800
Don't worry, it's not as scary as it sounds
— but it is harder than it looks to recreate

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.320
Marcus Henderson's fancy footwork in this
now-famous scene.

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.710
Casting controversies

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:17.030
Get Out has enjoyed nearly universal acclaim,
but leading man Daniel Kaluuya faced some

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.540
criticism from fellow actor Samuel L. Jackson:

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:25.709
"I tend to wonder, what would that movie have
been with an American brother who really feels

00:03:25.709 --> 00:03:26.709
that.”

00:03:26.709 --> 00:03:31.830
But Kaluuya responded by pushing back against
the false notion that he hasn't experienced

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:32.830
prejudice.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:36.850
In his words: "This is the frustrating thing,
bro — in order to prove that I can play

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:41.770
this role, I have to open up about the trauma
that I've experienced as a black person.

00:03:41.770 --> 00:03:45.430
I have to show off my struggle so that people
accept that I'm black.

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:50.600
No matter that every single room I go to I'm
usually the darkest person there.

00:03:50.600 --> 00:03:51.600
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.370
I kind of resent that mentality.

00:03:53.370 --> 00:03:54.650
I'm just an individual."

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.900
The hidden meaning of milk

00:03:56.900 --> 00:04:02.459
Allison Williams is a vision of pure evil
in this scene, scouting for new victims while

00:04:02.459 --> 00:04:05.590
eating Froot Loops and sipping from a tall
glass of milk.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.940
But two weeks before the movie came out, a
group of white supremacists did their part

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:16.150
to make this moment even creepier, when they
hijacked a political livestream by actor Shia

00:04:16.150 --> 00:04:20.930
LaBeouf and started chugging gallons of whole
milk to demonstrate their white pride.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:24.970
Jordan Peele wasn't aware when he wrote this
scene that milk would become such a fraught

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:29.160
symbol of racial hatred, but it definitely
upped the ante on the horror.

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:31.960
Jordan Peele has big plans for more horror

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:36.600
He might have started out in comedy, but Get
Out's director reportedly has a lot of ideas

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.520
for more movies in the genre he calls "social
thrillers":

00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:45.550
"You know these movies that are creepy, but
humanity is like the creepiest part at the

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.550
center of it."

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.620
Details of Peele's next project are still
under wraps, but he says he's got a whole

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:55.430
series of horror films in mind that will tackle
similar subject matter — and that's definitely

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:57.800
something for fans to scream about.

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.260
[Screaming]

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.500
Thanks for watching!

